        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "21abbd35-cb07-55c9-892c-da57aee7e08f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Quast, Colm Wilkinson, Michael Ball, Lea Salonga, Judy Kuhn, Ruthie Henshall, Michael Maguire, Alun Armstrong, Jenny Galloway, Adam Searles, Hannah Chick, John Caird, David Charles Abell, Sandra Sciberras, Victoria Thaine, Susie Porter, Adam Godley\n- Projects: Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert, The Caterpillar Wish\n- Organizations: Royal Philharmonic Orchestra\n- Places: London, Broadway, Australia\n- Roles: Jean Valjean, Inspector Javert, Marius Pontmercy, Éponine, Cosette, Fantine, Enjolras, Thénardier, Madame Thénardier, Gavroche, Young Cosette\n\nFacts:\n- Philip Quast was born on 30 July 1957 and is an Australian actor and singer.\n- The 10th Anniversary cast of Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert was chosen from the London, Broadway, and Australian productions of the show.\n- Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert starred Colm Wilkinson as Jean Valjean, Philip Quast as Inspector Javert, Michael Ball as Marius Pontmercy, Lea Salonga as Éponine, Judy Kuhn as Cosette, Ruthie Henshall as Fantine, Michael Maguire as Enjolras, Alun Armstrong as Thénardier, Jenny Galloway as Madame Thénardier, Adam Searles as Gavroche, and Hannah Chick as Young Cosette.\n- Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert was directed by John Caird, and the Royal Philharmonic Orchestra was conducted by David Charles Abell.\n- The Caterpillar Wish is a 2006 Australian coming-of-age film directed by Sandra Sciberras and featuring Victoria Thaine, Susie Porter, and Philip Quast in its ensemble cast.\n- Philip Quast has won the Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor in a Musical three times, which is the most of any actor to date.\n- Adam Godley is a Tony Award nominee and has received three Olivier Award nominations.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f8426986-2552-50e1-8024-3273c178482c",
        "text": "Page: Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert. Sentence: The 10th Anniversary cast stars Colm Wilkinson as Jean Valjean, Philip Quast as Inspector Javert, Michael Ball as Marius Pontmercy, Lea Salonga as Éponine, Judy Kuhn as Cosette, Ruthie Henshall as Fantine, Michael Maguire as Enjolras, Alun Armstrong as Thénardier, Jenny Galloway as Madame Thénardier, Adam Searles as Gavroche, Hannah Chick as Young Cosette, and several others, and was directed by John Caird.\nPage: Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert. Sentence: The performers were chosen from the London, Broadway and Australian productions of the show and the Royal Philharmonic Orchestra was conducted by David Charles Abell.\nPage: Philip Quast. Sentence: Philip Mark Quast (born 30 July 1957) is an Australian actor and singer.\nPage: Philip Quast. Sentence: He has won the Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor in a Musical three times, the most of any actor to date.\nPage: The Caterpillar Wish. Sentence: The Caterpillar Wish (also known as Caterpillar Wish) is a 2006 Australian coming-of-age film, directed by Sandra Sciberras and starring and ensemble cast including Victoria Thaine, Susie Porter and Philip Quast.\nPage: Adam Godley. Sentence: He is a Tony Award nominee and has been nominated three times for the Olivier Award.",
